  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>fitctree</keyword>
  <short_description>Fit a classification decision tree.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>mdl = fitctree(X, Y)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>mdl = fitctree(X, Y, Name, Value)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>label = predict(mdl, Xnew)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[label, score, cost, node] = predict(mdl, Xnew)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <description>
    <p><b>fitctree</b> creates a <b>ClassificationTree</b> object from numeric predictors <b>X</b> and class labels <b>Y</b>.</p>
    <p>Name-value arguments include <b>ClassNames</b>, <b>Prior</b>, <b>SplitCriterion</b>, <b>MaxNumSplits</b>, <b>MinLeafSize</b>, and <b>MinParentSize</b>. Numeric predictors are split with binary threshold tests. Prediction returns leaf class scores.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[X = [0 0; 0 1; 1 0; 1 1; 5 5; 5 6; 6 5; 6 6];
Y = [1; 1; 1; 1; 2; 2; 2; 2];
mdl = fitctree(X, Y);
[label, score] = predict(mdl, [0.2 0.1; 5.2 5.1])]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
